claim=dict(id='C_read_gate_release',kind='obligation',concern='implementation_semantics',description='A ReadOnlySafe request retained solely because its leader has not committed an entry in its current term must leave that pre-commit gate for normal read processing when the first current-term commitment is established. Configuration-driven commitment must not leave such a retained request gated on an additional log commitment.',source_ids=['S_pending_read_purpose','S_new_leader_read_test','S_read_api_contract','S_read_release','S_membership','S_early_advance_usage','S_node_advance_order','S_raw_advance_contract'],scope=dict(description='Pre-commit queue transition for a retained request on a nonsingleton leader, including commitment triggered by applying an already committed configuration. Synchronous Ready/Advance caller using the documented early-Advance optimization; actual application remains ordered.',assumptions=['Serialized RawNode methods, authentic peer messages and a stable leader during the measured transition.','Ready entries/HardState are persisted before Advance and messages; actual committed-entry application remains in log order.','The explicit package/Node permission to Advance after persistence while application is in progress applies through RawNode\'s documented correspondence to Node.','Unique request contexts, ReadOnlySafe, no process or storage crash.'],excluded=['Unconditional public ReadIndex completion; requests can be lost per API.','A time bound or general liveness result.','Linearizability violation, lease-based reads, concurrent context reuse and joint-configuration exhaustive coverage.']),pending=['Execute a fixed direct checker for pre-commit queue membership after the actual first-current-term transition.'],grounding=dict(source_ids=['S_proposal','S_read_release','S_membership','S_transition','S_ready','S_api'],expectation_ids=['S_pending_read_purpose','S_new_leader_read_test','S_early_advance_usage','S_node_advance_order','S_read_api_contract','S_raw_advance_contract'],derivation='S_pending_read_purpose states that these retained messages will be handled as soon as the first log entry is committed in the current term. S_new_leader_read_test expects the postponed request to be processed once that prerequisite is satisfied. The obligation is the internal prerequisite transition, not a stronger promise that all ReadIndex invocations complete. S_early_advance_usage says Advance may occur at any time after persistence and associates ApplyConfChange with application step 3; S_node_advance_order expressly allows in-progress application but prohibits out-of-order application. S_api states RawNode methods correspond to Node and are described more fully there. This gives an explicit source basis for the selected early-Advance interpretation, independent of the observed missing release.',applicability='The request is demonstrably retained in the pre-commit queue, rather than lost or not admitted. A legal quorum changes through application of a real committed configuration, and actual Ready work and heartbeat responses are delivered. No direct protocol-state assignments or timer-based deadline are needed.',conflicts=['S_raw_advance_contract describes Advance as applied-and-saved, whereas S_early_advance_usage and S_node_advance_order permit Advance before application finishes. The scope adopts the explicit optimization permission and keeps this documentation tension visible.'],alternatives=['Applying configuration before Advance keeps the campaign guard effective and avoids this particular prefix.','Public retry may produce a new successful read without discharging the originally retained queue entry; that does not prove the queue-transition contract.','An additional current-term proposal can later trigger the ordinary release path.'],unresolved=['A stricter interpretation requiring configuration activation before early Advance would exclude this prefix; correspondence review must adjudicate that interpretation from the captured API documentation.']))
